<title>UK: Morgan Crucible postpones Emblem float.</title>
<headline>Morgan Crucible postpones Emblem float.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Crucible has postponed the stock market flotation of its subsidiary Emblem Technology &quot;due to market conditions,&quot; a spokesman told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>The specialist engineering company, whose products are used in Harrier aircraft missile systems, was one of the companies being split off from the group.</p>
<p>The sponsor to the float was Panmure Gordon and Emblem was expected to have been valued at around 40.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Dealings in the shares were expected to begin this month.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
